<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="002" project="spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Author create-flow surface-launch capabilities (matter / Event-Task / To Do) + repoint shipped create-matter/create-task</title>
    <phase>1: Catalog &amp; Schema Foundation</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>none</dependencies>
    <blocks>010, 012, 021, 050</blocks>
    <tags>dataverse, ai, solution, fields</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Dispatch-catalog authoring + repointing shipped capabilities; drives grounded execution (ADR-039). Wrong routing breaks create flows.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Capability modeling + a net-new "capability launches a pre-seeded surface" mechanism decision; architectural judgment with correctness stakes.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Dataverse catalog authoring — main-session; co-designs the hand-off contract with task 012 (client side).</parallel-reason>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    RESOLVED 2026-07-15 (design §10.1, closes the earlier BLOCKED conflict): R1 create capabilities do NOT write records via a JPS — they DRAFT in chat then LAUNCH the entity's real create surface, pre-seeded. The shipped create-matter and create-task are disposition=Informational and have the LLM call dataverse.create_record directly (the multi-turn-elicitation dead-end). Repoint them to launch a surface, and split "task/to-do" intent by destination. Route by confirmed intent: matter → Create Matter wizard; Event-Task (sprk_event, subtype=Task) → Event wizard with subtype preset=Task; To Do (sprk_todo) → OOB sprk_todo create form in a modal. Author the tool descriptions + the "Event-Task vs To Do" ambiguity + chip transitions; author the surface-launch routing metadata the client hand-off (task 012) consumes.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE AI platform developer expert in the ADR-039 grounded-execution catalog (sprk_playbookconsumer Bindings, sprk_analysisaction Actions, tool descriptions, chip transitions, dispositions) and the client wizard/OOB-form launch surfaces.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Three create intents each dispatch to the correct pre-seeded launch surface (per design §10.1 routing table): (1) create-matter → Create Matter wizard; (2) create-event/Event-Task → Event wizard (subtype preset Task); (3) create-todo → OOB sprk_todo form modal. The shipped create-matter + create-task are repointed off direct dataverse.create_record onto the surface-launch hand-off. Each capability carries a tool description encoding the "Event-Task vs To Do" disambiguation + chip transitions. The surface-launch routing metadata (which surface + pre-seed contract) is authored so task 012's client hand-off can consume it.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      As-built (verified task 002, spaarkedev1): Binding = sprk_playbookconsumer joined to sprk_analysisaction. Shipped create-matter (UC-B-6) + create-task (UC-H-1) are disposition=Informational and instruct the LLM to call dataverse.create_record. create-task writes sprk_event(sprk_eventtype_ref="Task", recordId 124f5fc9-98ff-f011-8406-7c1e525abd8b). Both sprk_todo and sprk_event tables exist; no sprk_todo-writing capability exists. See BLOCKED.md (now resolved) + design §10.1.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/Binding.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerRoutingService.cs</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">ONE probabilistic decider; do NOT introduce a second intent mechanism when authoring the Event-Task-vs-To-Do ambiguity — it is authored into tool descriptions, not a classifier.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Route by design §10.1: matter→Create Matter wizard; Event-Task→Event wizard (subtype=Task preset); To Do→OOB sprk_todo form modal (Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo per MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA). Do NOT invent a sprk_todo-writing JPS; do NOT keep the LLM-calls-create_record path for these three intents.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The "capability launches a pre-seeded surface" mechanism is genuinely new: decide + document HOW a capability signals "open surface X pre-seeded" (candidate: a new sprk_disposition value or a new Binding column carrying the surface target) — this is the contract task 012 consumes; co-design it here (catalog side) with 012 (client side). If the mechanism choice needs an owner call (e.g. new disposition option-set value), surface it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Repoint (do not silently duplicate) the shipped create-matter + create-task rows. Preserve their sprk_consumertype identity where dispatch/consumers reference it; document the change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">The Event-Task / To Do records still honor their regarding contracts (11-entity regarding where applicable) — the wizard/OOB form owns the write; the capability only launches it pre-seeded.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Binding contract" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/Binding.cs">The full sprk_playbookconsumer + sprk_analysisaction field set + disposition/risk/surfaces vocabulary to author against.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Re-read the shipped create-matter + create-task rows (tooldescription, disposition, surfaces, action link) as the concrete baseline being repointed.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide + document the surface-launch mechanism (new disposition value vs new Binding column carrying the surface target + pre-seed contract). If it needs an owner call (option-set addition), surface it before authoring.</step>
    <step order="3">Author/repoint create-matter → launch Create Matter wizard, pre-seeded (file + drafted values via the task-012 envelope contract).</step>
    <step order="4">Author/repoint create-task → Event wizard with Event subtype preset = Task (sprk_event); update its tool description to the surface-launch behavior.</step>
    <step order="5">Author create-todo → OOB sprk_todo create form in a modal; tool description encodes the "explicit To Do" trigger.</step>
    <step order="6">Author the "Event-Task vs To Do" ambiguity into the tool descriptions (P4) + author sprk_chiptransitions rows for each.</step>
    <step order="7">List owed eval cases (task 051). Verify dispatch selects each capability for its trigger utterance (surface-open is verified in 012/013). Update TASK-INDEX.md 002 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the surface-launch mechanism requires a new sprk_disposition option-set value or other schema/option-set change needing owner sign-off, STOP and surface it (§6.5) before authoring — do not silently add an option-set value.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">Author/verify catalog rows (create/update sprk_playbookconsumer + sprk_analysisaction)</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/verify BFF if the mechanism touches Binding.cs / ConsumerRoutingService</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">Repointed create-matter + create-task rows; new create-todo row; surface-launch routing metadata; chip rows</output>
    <output type="notes" ephemeral="true">projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/notes/surface-launch-mechanism.md (the capability→surface hand-off contract 012 consumes)</output>
    <output type="notes" ephemeral="true">projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/notes/owed-eval-cases.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">"create a matter" dispatches a capability that launches the pre-seeded Create Matter wizard (not direct create_record).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"create a task"/"create an event" dispatches the Event-wizard launch with subtype preset = Task; "create a to do" dispatches the OOB sprk_todo form-modal launch.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Event-Task-vs-To-Do ambiguity resolves by inference or one-tap pick, never multi-turn text negotiation; encoded in tool descriptions only (no classifier).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The shipped create-matter + create-task are repointed off direct dataverse.create_record; the surface-launch routing metadata contract (for task 012) is documented; owed eval cases listed.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Spec FR-A2 / FR-A1 / P4; design §10.1. Was BLOCKED 2026-07-15 (as-built conflict) → resolved by owner decision (wizard/form-launch hand-off, intent-routed). Co-design the hand-off contract with task 012. Owner reviews content (FR-J1).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge/files before starting. /conflict-check before any BFF PR. FULL-rigor Step 9.5.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
